module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ConstantSheafFiniteness
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ConstantSheafModules

/-!
# Comparing a constant sheaf of modules with the constant sheaf of rings

Let `(C, J)` be a site and `Λ` a commutative ring. There are two constant sheaves attached to a
`Λ`-module `M` on `C`:

* the constant sheaf `(constantSheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)).obj M` in the category of sheaves of
  `Λ`-modules, whose sections over an object `U` carry a `Λ`-module structure and about which
  [Stacks, Tag 093J] says that `Γ(U, -)` is exact, and
* the constant sheaf of modules `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant.constantModuleSheaf J M` over the
  constant sheaf of rings `Λ̲ = (constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)`, whose sections
  over `U` carry a module structure over the *ring* `Γ(U, Λ̲)`.

Statements about an ideal sheaf cut out inside a sheaf of rings are about the second; the exactness
of `Γ(U, -)` is available only for the first. This file compares them on underlying sections, and
in the case `M = Λ` identifies the sections of the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `Λ` with the
sections of the constant sheaf of rings, in a way which turns the `Λ`-action into multiplication by
a section of `Λ̲`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantModuleSheafComparison`: the two constant sheaves have the same
  underlying sheaf of abelian groups, naturally in `M`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSectionsAddEquiv`: that comparison read on the sections over an
  object `U`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingSectionsAddEquiv`: the case `M = Λ`, composed with
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant.unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf`, so that the target is the ring
  `Γ(U, Λ̲)` itself.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingScalar`: the section of `Λ̲` over `U` by which an element of
  `Λ` acts under that comparison.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSectionsAddEquiv_map`: the comparison is natural in `M`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSectionsAddEquiv_smul`: the action of `a : Λ` on the sections of
  the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules becomes, under the comparison, the map of sections induced by
  `a • 𝟙 M`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_smul`: at `M = Λ` that map of sections is
  multiplication by `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingScalar J U a`. This is what carries a
  `Λ`-submodule of `Γ(U, Λ̲)` — such as the image of the sections of the constant sheaf on an ideal
  `I ⊂ Λ` — to an ideal of the ring `Γ(U, Λ̲)`, generated by the images of generators of `I`.

## Implementation notes

The comparison is assembled from two existing isomorphisms and no new sheaf theory. The sheaf of
abelian groups underlying `(constantSheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)).obj M` is the constant sheaf of
abelian groups on `M` because `forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w}` preserves
sheafification; this is Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.constantCommuteCompose`. The sheaf of abelian
groups underlying `constantModuleSheaf J M` is the same constant abelian sheaf *on the nose*,
which is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant.toSheafConstantIso`.

The last step for `M = Λ` is `unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf`, which identifies the constant sheaf of
modules on `Λ` with `SheafOfModules.unit Λ̲`, i.e. with `Λ̲` as a module over itself. Going
directly from the constant sheaf of *rings* to a constant abelian sheaf is not available: it would
need `forget₂ RingCat AddCommGrpCat` to preserve sheafification at an unrelated module universe,
which the pinned Mathlib does not provide. That is exactly why `unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf` is
proved by corepresentability, and why this file routes through it.

`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_smul` does not compute
`constantRingScalar J U a`; it only has to produce *some* section of `Λ̲` by which `a` acts, and
the argument that produces it is short. The induced endomorphism of sections is the restriction of
a morphism of sheaves of `Λ̲`-modules `SheafOfModules.unit Λ̲ ⟶ SheafOfModules.unit Λ̲`, hence is
`Γ(U, Λ̲)`-linear, and a `Γ(U, Λ̲)`-linear endomorphism of `Γ(U, Λ̲)` is multiplication by its
value at `1`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 093J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 093N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093N)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.ConstantSheaf

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
variable {Λ : Type w} [CommRing Λ]

section Comparison

variable [HasWeakSheafify J (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)]
  [J.PreservesSheafification (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J RingCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective RingCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- The sheaf of abelian groups underlying the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `M` is the sheaf
of abelian groups underlying the constant sheaf of `Λ̲`-modules on `M`, naturally in `M`.

Both are the constant sheaf of abelian groups on the additive group of `M`: for the first this is
`CategoryTheory.constantCommuteCompose` at `forget₂ (ModuleCat Λ) AddCommGrpCat`, for the second it
is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant.toSheafConstantIso`. -/
def constantModuleSheafComparison :
    constantSheaf J (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) ⋙
        sheafCompose J (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w}) ≅
      constantModuleSheafFunctor J (R := Λ) ⋙
        SheafOfModules.toSheaf ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)) :=
  constantCommuteCompose J (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w}) ≪≫
    (toSheafConstantIso J (R := Λ)).symm

/-- The comparison `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantModuleSheafComparison` read on the sections over
an object `U`: the sections of the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `M` and the sections of the
constant sheaf of `Λ̲`-modules on `M` are the same abelian group. -/
def constantSectionsAddEquiv (M : ModuleCat.{w} Λ) (U : C) :
    ((constantSections J U).obj M) ≃+ ((constantModuleSheaf J M).val.obj (op U)) :=
  Iso.addCommGroupIsoToAddEquiv
    (((sheafSections J AddCommGrpCat.{w}).obj (op U)).mapIso
      ((constantModuleSheafComparison J (Λ := Λ)).app M))

/-- The comparison of sections is natural in the module. -/
lemma constantSectionsAddEquiv_map {M N : ModuleCat.{w} Λ} (f : M ⟶ N) (U : C)
    (s : (constantSections J U).obj M) :
    constantSectionsAddEquiv J N U (((constantSections J U).map f).hom s) =
      (constantModuleSheafMap J f).val.app (op U) (constantSectionsAddEquiv J M U s) := by
  have h := ((sheafSections J AddCommGrpCat.{w}).obj (op U)).congr_map
    ((constantModuleSheafComparison J (Λ := Λ)).hom.naturality f)
  rw [Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp] at h
  exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h s

/-- Under the comparison of sections, the action of `a : Λ` on the sections of the constant sheaf
of `Λ`-modules on `M` is the map of sections induced by `a • 𝟙 M`. -/
lemma constantSectionsAddEquiv_smul (M : ModuleCat.{w} Λ) (U : C) (a : Λ)
    (s : (constantSections J U).obj M) :
    constantSectionsAddEquiv J M U (a • s) =
      (constantModuleSheafMap J (a • 𝟙 M)).val.app (op U)
        (constantSectionsAddEquiv J M U s) := by
  have hmap : ((constantSections J U).map (a • 𝟙 M)).hom s = a • s := by
    rw [Functor.map_smul, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
    rfl
  rw [← hmap, constantSectionsAddEquiv_map]

end Comparison

section Ring

variable [HasWeakSheafify J (ModuleCat.{w} Λ)]
  [J.PreservesSheafification (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{w} Λ) AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify J RingCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective RingCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- The sections over `U` of the constant sheaf of modules on `Λ`, compared with the sections of
`SheafOfModules.unit Λ̲`, i.e. with the ring `Γ(U, Λ̲)` itself. This is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant.unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf` read on sections. -/
def unitSectionsAddEquiv (U : C) :
    ((constantModuleSheaf J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)).val.obj (op U)) ≃+
      (((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U)) :=
  Iso.addCommGroupIsoToAddEquiv
    (((sheafSections J AddCommGrpCat.{w}).obj (op U)).mapIso
      ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ))).mapIso
        (unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf J (R := Λ)).symm))

/-- **The comparison between the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `Λ` and the constant sheaf of
rings on `Λ`, on sections.** The sections over `U` of the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules generated
by `Λ` are the same abelian group as the sections over `U` of the constant sheaf of rings generated
by `Λ`. -/
def constantRingSectionsAddEquiv (U : C) :
    ((constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)) ≃+
      (((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U)) :=
  (constantSectionsAddEquiv J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ) U).trans (unitSectionsAddEquiv J U)

/-- The section of the constant sheaf of rings over `U` by which `a : Λ` acts on the sections of
the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `Λ`, through
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingSectionsAddEquiv`. -/
def constantRingScalar (U : C) (a : Λ) :
    ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U) :=
  constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U (a • (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U).symm 1)

/-- The endomorphism of `SheafOfModules.unit Λ̲` induced by the action of `a : Λ` on the constant
sheaf of modules on `Λ`. -/
private def unitSmulEndo (a : Λ) :
    SheafOfModules.unit ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)) :=
  (unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf J (R := Λ)).hom ≫
    constantModuleSheafMap J (a • 𝟙 (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)) ≫
      (unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf J (R := Λ)).inv

/-- `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.unitSmulEndo` over an object `U`, read as a `Γ(U, Λ̲)`-linear
endomorphism of the ring `Γ(U, Λ̲)`. -/
private def unitSmulMap (U : C) (a : Λ) :
    ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U) →ₗ[
        ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U)]
      ((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U) :=
  ((unitSmulEndo J a).val.app (op U)).hom

private lemma constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_smul_aux (U : C) (a : Λ)
    (s : (constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)) :
    constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U (a • s) =
      unitSmulMap J U a (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U s) := by
  have hhom : ∀ t, unitSectionsAddEquiv J U t =
      ((unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf J (R := Λ)).inv.val.app (op U)).hom t := fun _ => rfl
  have hinv : ∀ t, (unitSectionsAddEquiv J U).symm t =
      ((unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf J (R := Λ)).hom.val.app (op U)).hom t := fun _ => rfl
  have hback : ((unitIsoConstantModuleSheaf J (R := Λ)).hom.val.app (op U)).hom
      (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U s) =
      constantSectionsAddEquiv J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ) U s := by
    rw [← hinv]
    exact (unitSectionsAddEquiv J U).symm_apply_apply _
  change unitSectionsAddEquiv J U
    (constantSectionsAddEquiv J (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ) U (a • s)) = _
  rw [constantSectionsAddEquiv_smul, hhom, ← hback]
  rfl

/-- **The `Λ`-action becomes multiplication by a section of the constant sheaf of rings.** Under
the comparison `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingSectionsAddEquiv`, multiplying a section of the
constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `Λ` by `a : Λ` corresponds to multiplying the corresponding
section of the constant sheaf of rings by `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingScalar J U a`. -/
theorem constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_smul (U : C) (a : Λ)
    (s : (constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)) :
    constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U (a • s) =
      constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U s * constantRingScalar J U a := by
  rw [constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_smul_aux, constantRingScalar,
    constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_smul_aux, AddEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  have h := (unitSmulMap J U a).map_smul (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U s) 1
  rwa [smul_eq_mul, mul_one, smul_eq_mul] at h

/-- `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantRingScalar J U a` is the image under the comparison of `a` times
the preimage of `1`. -/
lemma constantRingScalar_eq (U : C) (a : Λ) :
    constantRingScalar J U a =
      constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U (a • (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U).symm 1) :=
  rfl

/-- The scalar of `0` is `0`. -/
@[simp]
lemma constantRingScalar_zero (U : C) : constantRingScalar J U (0 : Λ) = 0 := by
  rw [constantRingScalar_eq, zero_smul, map_zero]

/-- The scalar of a sum is the sum of the scalars. -/
lemma constantRingScalar_add (U : C) (a b : Λ) :
    constantRingScalar J U (a + b) =
      constantRingScalar J U a + constantRingScalar J U b := by
  rw [constantRingScalar_eq, constantRingScalar_eq, constantRingScalar_eq, add_smul, map_add]

/-- The scalar of a product is the product of the scalars. -/
lemma constantRingScalar_mul (U : C) (a b : Λ) :
    constantRingScalar J U (a * b) =
      constantRingScalar J U a * constantRingScalar J U b := by
  have h : (a * b) • (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U).symm 1 =
      b • (a • (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J (Λ := Λ) U).symm 1) := by
    rw [← mul_smul, mul_comm]
  rw [constantRingScalar_eq J U (a * b), h, constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_smul,
    ← constantRingScalar_eq]

/-- The ideal of `Γ(U, Λ̲)` generated by the scalars of a `Λ`-submodule of `Λ` is generated by the
scalars of any spanning set of that submodule: `a ↦ constantRingScalar J U a` is additive and
multiplicative, so it carries a `Λ`-linear combination to a `Γ(U, Λ̲)`-linear combination. -/
lemma span_constantRingScalar_image_span (U : C) (t : Set Λ) :
    Submodule.span (((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U))
        (constantRingScalar J U '' (Submodule.span Λ t : Set Λ)) =
      Submodule.span (((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U))
        (constantRingScalar J U '' t) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (Submodule.span_mono (Set.image_mono Submodule.subset_span))
  rw [Submodule.span_le]
  rintro x ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
  induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem z hz => exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩
  | zero => rw [constantRingScalar_zero]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add p q _ _ ihp ihq =>
      rw [constantRingScalar_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ ihp ihq
  | smul r p _ ih =>
      rw [smul_eq_mul, constantRingScalar_mul, ← smul_eq_mul]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ih

/-- **Finite generation of the ideal of scalars of a finitely generated ideal.** If `I ⊂ Λ` is
finitely generated then the ideal of the ring `Γ(U, Λ̲)` generated by the scalars of `I` is
finitely generated, by the scalars of any finite generating set of `I`. -/
theorem fg_span_constantRingScalar_image (I : Ideal Λ) (hI : I.FG) (U : C) :
    (Submodule.span (((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U))
      (constantRingScalar J U '' (I : Set Λ))).FG := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hI
  rw [← hs, span_constantRingScalar_image_span]
  exact Submodule.fg_span (s.finite_toSet.image _)

/-- **The transport of `I · Γ(U, Λ̲)` into the sections of the constant sheaf of rings.** A section
of the constant sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `Λ` lying in `I · Γ(U, Λ̲)` is carried by the comparison
into the ideal of `Γ(U, Λ̲)` generated by the scalars of `I`. -/
theorem mem_span_constantRingScalar_of_mem_smul_top (I : Ideal Λ) (U : C)
    {t : (constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)}
    (ht : t ∈ I • (⊤ : Submodule Λ ((constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ)))) :
    constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U t ∈
      Submodule.span (((constantSheaf J RingCat.{w}).obj (RingCat.of Λ)).obj.obj (op U))
        (constantRingScalar J U '' (I : Set Λ)) := by
  refine Submodule.smul_induction_on ht ?_ ?_
  · intro a ha x _
    rw [constantRingSectionsAddEquiv_smul, ← smul_eq_mul]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩)
  · intro x y hx hy
    rw [map_add]
    exact Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy

/-- The converse inclusion to `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.mem_span_constantRingScalar_of_mem_smul_top` on
generators: the scalar of an element of `I` is the image of an element of `I · Γ(U, Λ̲)`. -/
theorem constantRingScalar_mem_image (I : Ideal Λ) (U : C) {a : Λ} (ha : a ∈ I) :
    constantRingScalar J U a ∈ constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U ''
      (I • (⊤ : Submodule Λ ((constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of Λ Λ))) : Set _) :=
  ⟨a • (constantRingSectionsAddEquiv J U).symm 1,
    Submodule.smul_mem_smul ha Submodule.mem_top, rfl⟩

end Ring

end Stacks.ConstantSheaf

end
